<statement>
<p>
Consider the routine below checks whether the input myArray contains three elements, a, b, and c such that a + b = c. Determine the run-time complexity of the routine using Big-O notation.
</p>
<p>
  def check<underscore/>for<underscore/>sum<underscore/>triplet(myArray): </p>
<p>
    for element<underscore/>a in myArray: </p>
<p>
      for element<underscore/>b in myArray: </p>
<p>
        for element<underscore/>c in myArray: </p>
<p>
          if element<underscore/>a + element<underscore/>b == element<underscore/>c:</p>
<p>
            return TRUE
  </p>
<p>
    return FALSE
</p>
<p>
The algorithm as written above has a run-time complexity of </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}^{{3}}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({2}^{{n}}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}!\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({1}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}^{{2}}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}\right)}</m></li> 
<li><m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({\log{{\left({n}\right)}}}\right)}</m></li> 
</ol></p>
 

</statement>
<solution>
<p><ul><li>A: <m>\displaystyle{O}{\left({n}^{{3}}\right)}</m></li></ul></p>
</solution>
</myopenmath>

